            <ArticleTitle>Visible-Light Driven Photocascade Catalysis: Union of N,N-Dimethylanilines and α-Azidochalcones in Flow Microreactors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2249-2256</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.joc.6b02932</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>N,N-Dimethylanilines were coupled with α-azidochalcones using visible-light driven Ru(bpy)3(PF6)2 catalyzed photocascade continuous flow microfluidic approach that involves the creation of one C-C and two C-N new bonds. The reaction involves dual photocatalysis ensuing two sp3 C-H bond functionalization of N,N-dimethylanilines. To explore the scope of the reaction, 20 different 1,3-diazabicyclo[3.1.0]hexanes were synthesized in good yields (55-71%).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
